Expected elements: present

Slim identity bar with `← aztec` exiting to the chain, `0xb63616…6359`, `Partial`, `block 101`, eight stepping buttons covering both directions, scrubber, `128 / 1315` and the phase rail; `CODE` positioned at line 32; `CALL TRACE | EVENT LOG` as one tab strip, Call Trace open, seven frames; `VALUES` a pane below it, not a tab; `TRANSACTION` with `DATA` / `Synthetic demo data` / the producer's sentences. No band above the bar, no explorer chrome, no spinner.

This is the desktop app's register. Pane vocabulary matches it word for word, the editor palette is the real one, the branch marks in the gutter belong to that editor's language, and the current position is drawn identically in Code and Call Trace — one cyan left rail plus row fill in both panes. Removing the band improved the register: nothing now interrupts the panes.

Two things do not belong. `Status reason: private-part-succeeded-public-part-succeeded` is an internal enum printed at the top of the Transaction pane, in a product whose copy is otherwise written for people, and it is the only unlabelled row in a labelled pane. And the identity bar's right half is a run of unlike objects — bar, sentence, fraction, segmented rail — stating the engine's load twice in two idioms, with 337 px of empty bar sitting to their right.

Fixes: write the status reason as a sentence; group or separate the bar's status cluster and move the scrubber away from `Engine loading`.

Rating: 7/10

